// === OF KINGDOMS, COURTS, AND IMPROBABLE WEATHER ===
hp_location
  // --- WITHIN YE STORYBOOK CASTLE ---
  Location: a sunlit gilded throne room crowded with richly dressed courtiers, royal guards, velvet banners, tall columns, and glowing stained-glass windows.
  Location: a vast castle banquet hall filled with noble guests, long wooden tables, silver dishes, flowering garlands, bright tapestries, and hundreds of candles.
  Location: a luminous royal chapel with carved stone arches, colorful stained glass, ceremonial flowers, golden details, and rows of gathered courtiers.
  Location: a grand castle staircase with carved balustrades, heraldic banners, flowering vines, red carpet, and tall arched windows filled with daylight.
  Location: a bright royal bedchamber with a carved canopy bed, embroidered curtains, painted chests, fresh flowers, and warm sunlight pouring through open windows.
  Location: a ceremonial castle armory with polished shields, jeweled swords, gleaming suits of armor, royal banners, and bright torchlight reflected on pale stone walls.

  // --- OF PALACE GROUNDS AND GARDENS MOST FAIR ---
  Location: a storybook palace garden with rose-covered arches, marble fountains, flowering hedges, white peacocks, and a brilliant rainbow across the sky.
  Location: a winding royal hedge maze beneath dramatic storm clouds, with white statues, flowering paths, and distant lightning beyond the palace towers.
  Location: a bustling castle courtyard filled with servants, white horses, royal guards, flower-covered balconies, and colorful banners moving in the wind.
  Location: a swan lake beneath pale palace towers, with carved stone steps, drifting flower petals, flowering reeds, and two rainbows reflected in the water.
  Location: a high castle terrace overlooking forests, villages, waterfalls, and distant mountains beneath a bright sky filled with sunlit clouds.

  // --- OF CROWDED STREETS, FESTIVALS, AND GREAT COMMOTION ---
  Location: a crowded medieval market street beneath colorful banners, filled with merchants, musicians, flower sellers, animals, wooden stalls, and townspeople in festival clothing.
  Location: a bustling Renaissance festival filled with striped tents, flower garlands, costumed crowds, jugglers, musicians, dancers, and heraldic flags.
  Location: a packed castle gate during a royal procession, with mounted guards, decorated horses, trumpeters, waving banners, and cheering citizens pressed along the road.
  Location: a crowded village square during a midsummer celebration, with flower crowns, ribboned poles, musicians, dancers, lanterns, and a rainbow appearing after warm rain.
  Location: a kingdom street during pouring rain, crowded with cloaked townspeople, colorful awnings, running horses, overflowing gutters, and palace towers flashing beneath distant lightning.
  Location: a snowy medieval street crowded with cloaked townspeople, market stalls, glowing windows, decorated evergreen branches, and thick snow falling around distant castle towers.
  Location: a crowded bridge leading toward a hilltop castle, filled with pilgrims, merchants, guards, wagons, flower sellers, and royal banners beneath a bright storybook sky.

  // --- OF ROYAL CEREMONY AND SPECTACLE ---
  Location: a magnificent coronation hall crowded with nobles, clergy, guards, musicians, and attendants beneath raised banners, golden columns, and glowing stained glass.
  Location: a grand masked palace ball filled with richly dressed guests, musicians, dancers, flower garlands, crystal chandeliers, and open windows showing a moonlit rainbow.
  Location: a royal tournament surrounded by striped pavilions, heraldic tents, armored competitors, decorated horses, wooden stands, and cheering crowds.
  Location: a flower-covered royal wedding pavilion beside a castle, crowded with courtiers, musicians, attendants, white doves, silk banners, and falling rose petals.
  Location: a royal balcony during a grand parade, with trumpeters, waving banners, flower petals, decorated rooftops, and enormous cheering crowds filling the streets below.
